{#-
  CLAUDE.md master template.
  Owns all top-level structure. Library files supply slot content.
  A section disappears entirely if its data is empty.

  Variables in scope:
    bot                — BotConfig with .name, .telegram, .scope, etc.
    fleet              — FleetConfig
    title_label        — string, derived from first expertise file's frontmatter
    expertise_body     — string, concatenated expertise file bodies
    voice              — None or { name, body }
    teams              — list of TeamConfig (only if bot is a manager)
    resources          — list of { title, description, body }
    integrations       — list of { title, description, body }
    principles         — list of { title, description, body }
    protocols          — list of { title, description, body }
    guardrails         — list of { title, description, body }
    lessons            — list of { title, description, body }
    post_actions       — list of { title, description, body }
-#}
# {{ bot.name }}{% if title_label %} — {{ title_label }}{% endif %}

{% if voice -%}
## Voice: {{ voice.title }}

{{ voice.body }}

{% endif -%}
{{ expertise_body }}

{%- if bot.mission %}

## Mission

{{ bot.mission | trim }}
{% endif -%}

{%- if bot.scope %}

## Scope

{% if bot.scope.org -%}
- **Org:** `{{ bot.scope.org }}`
{% endif -%}
{% if bot.scope.repos -%}
- **Repos:** {{ bot.scope.repos | map('quote_backtick') | join(', ') }}
{% endif -%}
{% if bot.scope.snowflake_targets -%}
- **Snowflake targets:** {{ bot.scope.snowflake_targets | map('quote_backtick') | join(', ') }}
{% endif -%}
{% for k, v in bot.scope.raw.items() -%}
- **{{ k }}:** {{ v }}
{% endfor %}
Operate exclusively within this scope. If a task targets resources outside it, surface to the human before acting.
{% endif -%}

{%- if bot.telegram.handle %}

## Telegram Identity

- **Your handle:** `@{{ bot.telegram.handle }}`
- **Your requireMention setting:** `{{ bot.telegram.require_mention }}`
{% if bot.telegram.require_mention -%}
- **This means:** ONLY respond to messages that @-mention `@{{ bot.telegram.handle }}` or reply to one of your own messages. Stay silent on all other group messages, even if they seem relevant to you.
{% else -%}
- **This means:** You see every group message. Stay silent if it @-mentions another bot or replies to another bot's message. Respond to generic messages, messages addressed to the group, or messages that name you.
{% endif -%}
{% endif -%}

{%- if bot.model_strategy %}

## Model Strategy

{% if bot.model_strategy.base -%}
- **Base model:** `{{ bot.model_strategy.base }}`
{% endif -%}
{% if bot.model_strategy.escalate_to -%}
- **Escalate to:** `{{ bot.model_strategy.escalate_to }}` — {{ bot.model_strategy.escalate_when or 'when work exceeds base capacity' }}
{% endif -%}
{% if bot.model_strategy.compact_when -%}
- **Compact when:** {{ bot.model_strategy.compact_when }}
{% endif %}
{% endif -%}

{%- if teams %}

## Fleet You Manage

{% for team in teams -%}
### Team: {{ team.name }}

| Bot | Expertise | Model | tmux | Telegram |
|-----|-----------|-------|------|----------|
{% for worker_name in team.workers -%}
{% set worker = fleet.bots.get(worker_name) -%}
{% if worker -%}
| {{ worker_name }} | {{ worker.expertise | join(', ') }} | {{ worker.model or '(default)' }} | {{ worker_name }} | {% if worker.telegram.handle %}@{{ worker.telegram.handle }}{% else %}—{% endif %} |
{% else -%}
| {{ worker_name }} | (undefined) | — | {{ worker_name }} | — |
{% endif -%}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}

{%- macro render_section(label, items) -%}
{% if items %}

## {{ label }}

{% for item in items -%}
### {{ item.title }}

{{ item.body | trim }}

{% endfor -%}
{% endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

